:: Carter Pool Swimming Relax and Chat [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>
While splashing around is fun and all, it also tires you out pretty quickly. So, you both decide to just relax on some of the pool floaties for a minute to catch your breath and recover some energy for more fun to come. You lie on a bright blue mattress floatie, leaning back with your hands behind your head and your legs crossed. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> chose his own personal floatie, one designed like a pepperoni pizza. <span style="color:Pink">It is pretty cute and, honestly with how small <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is, you both could have fitted on it. Maybe another time.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Swim",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Isn’t this great?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Just relaxing, having fun. Super chill!”</span> You can’t help but snort at him saying that, finding his attempt to be cool adorable. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I mean it! Just swimming without Kohler telling us to do laps or underwater jumping jacks. And no one else trying to be funny or splash you. It’s nice.”</span> You agree, finding the gentle swaying of the water pretty relaxing. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightGreen">As you are both just chilling there, you think about bringing up a topic of conversation, turning to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> to ask him a question.</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
	<<link "Ask about how he learned to swim<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> how he learned to swim. You figured he wouldn’t be the best at it, considering… <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Considering!?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> turns to you, sounding slightly offended, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m great at swimming! Well, in a pool at least. Still have trouble when there’s waves and stuff.”</span> He chuckles nervously, no doubt recalling a time his tiny body was swept away by the waves, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s kinda funny actually. I learned a few years ago by accident.”</span> Intrigued, you ask him for the story. <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Smirk",
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Carter",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Swim",
                        Mouth: "Happy",
                        Blush: 1,
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, we were having a barbeque with some of my dad’s friends from work. I had gotten out of the pool to eat, took my floaties off and stuff. I was so excited to get back in and play that I sorta just jumped in without them.”</span> He laughs. You ask if someone had to jump in and save him and he shakes his head. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No. Well, I’m sure they would have if they’d noticed. But I didn’t even! I sorta just… swam? Like, no floaties or anything. I didn’t even realize I was doing it by myself until <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> suddenly pointed it out.”</span> <br>
        <br>
        You nod along, calling it pretty impressive. It’s kind of like those stories about dad’s throwing their kids into the water to see if they sink or swim, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> sort of did it to himself. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah, haha.”</span> He laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Mom was a little freaked out once she found out I jumped in without thinking, but her and Dad were also super proud I did it! I did get in a little bit of trouble though, but I guess that’s fair. Better safe than sorry, even if it all turned out alright!”</span> <br>
        <span style="color:green">+Carter Comfort</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Comfort += 5>>
        <span style="color:Green">+Carter Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
        <<socialChange "Carter" 1>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Carter House Backyard Swim]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
	<<link "Ask about the yard<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> how he got so lucky with a backyard like this. A pool, trampoline, even a tree house! He must be great at the puppy dog eyes. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No, haha. Well, I guess I am? But I mostly beg for collectables and comics and stuff.”</span> That is true, he does have a scary amount of those, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Most of the stuff out here wasn’t actually me. The pool and jungle gym came with the house, and mom and dad bought it before I was born! The trampoline was a birthday gift for <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> forever ago.”</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Happy",
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Carter",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Swim",
                        Mouth: "Happy",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“The treehouse though was my idea.”</span> He smiles, pointing to it, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“A few summers back after some stuff, Dad promised me we could all do a project together. Like all of us. So, I thought it be cool to build a tree house! We all worked together for a few weeks and made the best treehouse ever! If the weather is nice enough, I even camp out there sometimes. Maybe we can try it during a sleepover!”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightGreen">He sounds pretty excited about the idea, clearly proud of his treehouse. You agree that would be pretty fun, internally thinking about all the fun you two could get up to there.</span> <br>
        <span style="color:green">+Carter Comfort</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Comfort += 5>>
        <span style="color:Green">+Carter Energy</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Energy += 30>>
        <span style="color:Green">+Carter Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
        <<socialChange "Carter" 1>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Carter House Backyard Swim]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<if $HangOutNeed.Comfort > 50>>
        <<link "Ask if he ever swam naked<br>">>
        <<replace "#choice">>
            <span style="color:Pink">With a smirk, you ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> if he’s ever swam naked before. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> immediately blushes at this,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Wha-!? Why would I do that!?”</span> He asks with embarrassment. You laugh, stating that how could he not? Private pool all to himself. He’s had to try it at least once! <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No way! I’m not allowed to swim alone, so <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> or my dad or someone is always with me. I can’t swim naked in front of them!”</span> <span style="color:Pink">You point out that he’s clearly ended up naked in the pool on multiple occasions, considering what you’ve seen. So how is a bit of skinny dipping any different?</span> <br>

                <<set _ad to [
                    {
                        Name: "Player",
                        State: {
                            Mouth: "Smirk",
                            Eyes: "Tired",
                        },
                    },
                    {
                        Name: "Carter",
                        State: {
                            Outfit: "Swim",
                            Mouth: "Frown",
                            Eyes: "Mad",
                            Blush: 1,
                        },
                    },
                ]>>
                <<ad _ad>>

            <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Because those weren’t on purpose!”</span> He responds, crossing his arms and turning away as you chuckle. There is a brief moment of silence before <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> turns back and shyly says, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But I do swim in my underwear sometimes. Like, when it’s super hot in the summer.”</span> He blushes more as you smile, claiming you’d love to see that. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No way! I’ve only done that with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>, and only because he does it first! It is kinda fun though…”</span> <span style="color:Pink">You chuckle, leaning back as you imagine <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> swimming around in his little briefs, wet and clinging to his body. That would be a sight to see.</span> <br>
            <span style="color:Green">+Carter Energy</span><br>
            <<set $HangOutNeed.Energy += 30>>
            <span style="color:Green">+Carter Fun</span><br>
            <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
            <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
            <<socialChange "Carter" 1>>
            <br>
            [[Continue|Carter House Backyard Swim]]
        <</replace>>
        <</link>>
    <<else>>
        <span style="color:red">Ask if he ever swam naked</span><br>
